"""Hand-written data for the period pages (/art-movements/<slug>), built by build_pages.py.

The plan (strategy/art-suite.md in the company repo) calls for period pages linked from the
movements guide. These are the movements with real search demand and enough public-domain works
in the catalog to show properly (Ahrefs US, Nov 2026, monthly volume and KD):
  renaissance art 38K KD 6, renaissance paintings 24K KD 0, baroque art 21K KD 6,
  pointillism 19K KD 17, fauvism 18K KD 37, rococo art 12K KD 26, realism art 11K KD 22,
  mannerism 11K KD 14, ukiyo-e 9.9K KD 45, neoclassicism 9.1K KD 31, post impressionism 8.5K KD 29,
  impressionist paintings 7K KD 5, hudson river school 4.2K KD 12, northern renaissance 3.4K KD 6,
  romanticism paintings 2.7K KD 8, symbolism art 2.3K KD 6.
Left out: the Dutch Golden Age (200 searches a month), the Pre-Raphaelites, Expressionism and Art
Nouveau (too few reliable public-domain works), and movements after about 1910 (mostly in copyright).

Dates, places, key artists and "how to recognize it" come from art_movements.py, so the guide and
the pages agree. Histories and questions are written here. Works follow the same rules as the
artist pages: only records from museums' open data, the curated wiki- set or hand-checked entries.
"""

